commit ec3dbf6b68dc3bc80680a18eed939bbbed0ce697

C03: the screen-reading scope exemption covers identifying buttons, and a stated line count must be the recognized one (SCREEN1811)

SCREEN1809 measured: every faithful draft for «tomá un screenshot, identificá el botón» («No puedo identificar botones en imágenes, sólo leer el texto de la pantalla…») was vetoed as an asserted failure because the scope exemption of the failure lens (mind and App) only covered describing or seeing images; and the English variant said «the screen shows 3 lines», counting the excerpt. The exemption now covers identificar/reconocer botones and identify/recognize buttons; a screen-reading final whose prose states a number other than seen.lineCount is a screen_wrong_count defect with its own hint; «líneas y escribe:» copied from the lens is a copied instruction.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>


